  + [profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-entry-stability/0.1
  + [status] is authorized_pending_implementation

& [Steps] are exact
  + [step_1] verify exact source hash, byte count, manifest, architecture selection, and current assembly signature
  + [step_2] complete delineation, semantic refinement, inward depth, subcomponent weaving, cross-weaving, constraint checking, pruning, data design, and seven-fold exhaustion
  + [step_3] issue separate explosion, canonical specification, justification, plan, registry, matrix, slice, and governing satisfaction signature
  + [step_4] implement one pure module and one exact library export with no dependency or unsafe delta
  + [step_5] add focused unit tests for strict decoding, both nested fault sides, syntax identities, all eight first differences, output preservation, and deterministic repeatability
  + [step_6] add one independent static no-effect and anti-provenance surface test
  + [step_7] run focused debug and overflow-checked release verification
  + [step_8] generate clone-portable evidence and run evidence rehash tests in both profiles
  + [step_9] run workspace debug and overflow-checked release tests plus format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, and dependency audit
  + [step_10] publish solution, proof, completion review, narrative, reentry, registry, matrix, slice, and file-change attribution

& [Checkpoints] are mandatory
  + [authority_checkpoint] every processed SJS stage is path, section, and hash bound before code
  + [implementation_checkpoint] only authorized files change and Cargo, lockfile, unsafe, platform-call, and effect deltas remain zero
  + [focused_checkpoint] every requirement and failure class has a direct test or static proof edge
  + [global_checkpoint] current workspace behavior and recursive evidence remain valid
  + [completion_checkpoint] support_delta and requirement_delta are reviewed before selecting another slice

& [StopRules] are fail closed
  + stop on source, manifest, architecture, prerequisite signature, or artifact-binding mismatch
  + stop if either nested input can bypass the current assembly transform
  + stop if identities or role labels are described as physical provenance or order
  + stop if any admitted observation field lacks an explicit comparison or separate syntax gate
  + stop if comparison becomes tolerant, unordered, normalized, scored, probabilistic, or learned
  + stop if stable output loses either source observation or releases with a fault
  + stop on dependency, unsafe, platform, filesystem, process, environment, clock, network, persistence, model, content-read, traversal, Git, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, or promotion behavior
